      },
      "lineNbr": 367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T20:23:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t in practice: only if the test process died between fork() and prctl(). PR_SET_PDEATHSIG was redundant too: the harness kills the test\u0027s whole process group on a timeout, and a worker waiting at the handshake reads EOF once the test process is gone. Removed both.",
      "parentUuid": "5681887f_43e1c06f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 366,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 367,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5308fa67f46e63fd67b5ae10091ca81979acf5c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
