      "lineNbr": 915,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T17:58:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`worker_exit()` uncondtionally exits with status code 0, so how can the parent tell that this is different from success? Actually, it seems like the parent would just get stuck waiting forever, no?",
      "revId": "5308fa67f46e63fd67b5ae10091ca81979acf5c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92d4d965_71a40f1a",
        "filename": "tools/testing/selftests/drivers/wrapfd/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 915,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T20:23:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The exit status isn\u0027t how the failure is reported: a failed EXPECT_*() in the worker writes KSFT_FAIL into the test metadata, which is shared (MAP_SHARED), so the test fails whatever the worker\u0027s exit status. worker_exit() clears the trigger so that the test process\u0027s next ASSERT_*() doesn\u0027t fire. The test process can\u0027t hang either: it holds no write end of the ready pipe, so when a worker exits early, worker_wait_ready() reads EOF and fails with \"worker N exited before it was ready\".",
      "parentUuid": "bb7a1c0f_29297b49",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5308fa67f46e63fd67b5ae10091ca81979acf5c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
